WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.514
Patrasche stopped at the gates of the cathedral.

2
00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:11.008
He had waited here many times while Nello gazed at the beautiful paintings inside.

3
00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:15.954
The tall gates had been blown open by the wind.

4
00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:21.172
Patrasche crept through the gates and up to the cathedral doors.

5
00:00:21.173 --> 00:00:27.298
It was long after midnight, and the huge wooden doors were closed.

6
00:00:27.299 --> 00:00:34.492
The Christmas Eve worshippers who had gone to midnight mass had gone home.

7
00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:39.302
Patrasche tried to push open one of the tall doors.

8
00:00:39.303 --> 00:00:41.634
It was locked.

9
00:00:41.635 --> 00:00:44.076
He tried another one.

10
00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.502
It was shut too.

11
00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:50.183
He walked around the side of the cathedral.

12
00:00:50.184 --> 00:00:57.556
There he found a door someone had forgotten to lock, and he pushed his way inside.

13
00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.909
The cathedral was almost empty.

14
00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:07.424
As Patrasche walked along the stone floor, snow fell from his fur.

15
00:01:07.425 --> 00:01:11.326
He left a little trail of snow behind him.

16
00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:15.744
Patrasche saw a figure lying in front of the altar.

17
00:01:15.745 --> 00:01:18.330
It was Nello.

18
00:01:18.331 --> 00:01:23.553
Patrasche crept up and put his paw on Nello's head.

19
00:01:23.554 --> 00:01:29.145
Nello cried out softly and grabbed Patrasche gently.

20
00:01:29.146 --> 00:01:33.941
"Let us lie down and die together," he murmured.

21
00:01:33.942 --> 00:01:38.882
"No one needs us, and we are all alone."

22
00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:43.556
Patrasche put his head upon the young boy's chest.

23
00:01:43.557 --> 00:01:48.486
There were great tears in the dog's sad brown eyes.

24
00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:53.827
The two friends lay close together in the freezing air.

25
00:01:53.828 --> 00:01:59.072
The cathedral's stone floor was as cold as snow.

26
00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:03.508
They fell asleep, and together they dreamed.

27
00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:16.153
They dreamed of happier days─when they chased each other through the fields, played with little Alois, or watched boats sail on the canal.

28
00:02:16.154 --> 00:02:22.048
Suddenly, pale rays of white light broke through the darkness.

29
00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:24.644
It was the moon.

30
00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:29.807
The snow had stopped falling and the clouds had slipped

31
00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:38.106
away. The moon's light shone through the high windows in the cathedral's

32
00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:44.330
arches. Rubens' great paintings looked down on the still bodies on the stone

33
00:02:44.331 --> 00:02:50.077
floor. Curtains usually covered the two pictures on either side of the

34
00:02:50.078 --> 00:02:56.561
altar. When Nello had first entered in the dark, he had pulled the curtains

35
00:02:56.562 --> 00:03:04.105
aside. The two paintings were Rubens' The Elevation of the Cross and The Descent from the

36
00:03:04.106 --> 00:03:08.653
Cross. For one moment, they were both visible in the

37
00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:11.214
moonlight. Nello stood

38
00:03:11.215 --> 00:03:16.021
